Here is one unique TOP-Game, one that really nobodoy should miss. After finishing the Main Campaign (about 20 hours, and we are talking about a "beat'em up" game), I was completely ecstasized: the gameplay is really perfect, with wonderful Boss Fight; the plot is Naruto Plot, and so a true Masterpiece by Masashi Kishimoto (great man).
And ... once you have finished the game (and so unlocked all the characters) you have 81 playable characters (lot of them, with 2 or more costumes and different "Finish Moves") plus 7 support characters to use in various modality: VS, Tournament and, above all, the marvellous "Survival" (that you unlock only completing a secondary Quest after finishing the Main Plot).
What, instead, I really didn't like are the dubbing SYNC (awful, both in English and in Japanese: the voices speak ALWAYS before the lip animations end, and this is an unforgivable shame because all the actors made a great job) and one absurd choice about sound effects: if you use a "Finish Move" without killing the enemy, there are not impact sounds!
And here is my numerical evaluation:
- Main Plot = 10/10;
- Secondary Quests = 8/10;
- Characters = 9/10;
- Gameplay = 10/10;
- Video (Graphic and cut scenes) = 8,5/10;
- Animations = 18/10 (yes, I said 18!!! Simply the BEST Game ever made);
- Audio (Dubbing) = 2/10 (only because of the awful dubbing sync);
- Sound Effects = 8,5/10;
- Musics = 9/10.
Global = 9/10 (it is not an arithmetic mean).

This game is an I don't even. What is there to say about this game? I'll tell you. "What? What?? WHAT?!?!?!" I like this game. It's a fun game. It reminds me of Doom. It reminds me of Doom. It reminds me of Doom. Guys, spoiler alert, Doom is a million times better than this. If you have to choose between ANY Doom game and this, pick Doom. In all seriousness, the game has a similar feel to such classics as Hard Reset, Galactic Hitman, Alpha Prime, and Halo. Only one of these is a classic, but let me explain why this game isn't garbage. It was made in Unity like Galactic Hitman, that review is a journey in itself; there are a bunch of enemies that seem too great in numbers to actually make sense.  The map has a first map of Halo type of feel, which is fairly similar to Alpha Prime and Space Hack.  A spaceship that got ♥♥♥♥ed up, and you gotta fight through it.  The gunplay feels a bit like Hard Reset, it is not the same system, however I got the same sort of vibe when I pulled the trigger. The graphics aren't stellar (that's a pun, because space;
), but it isnt much worse than Half Life: Source.
Have fun!

